From febaa6c9f47a64420c15cf8c8409627b6dbd77c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 08:53:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 259/273] drm/sun4i: de3: Make channel CSC aware of the output
 format and encoding

When the display engine outputs YUV, every channel has to be converted
to the output color space before blending, not just YUV ones. Select
the channel CSC conversion table based on the framebuffer format, the
plane's own encoding/range, and the engine's negotiated output format
and encoding:
- RGB planes get an RGB to YUV conversion when the output is YUV,
  targeting whatever encoding (BT.601/709/2020) the engine actually
  negotiated,
- YUV planes get an encoding/range conversion to the output encoding,
- conversions to RGB output are unchanged.

Conversion tables are taken from the vendor driver, same as existing
ones.

UI channels were purely RGB so far and had no CSC unit wired up. Set
their CSC units up on DE3 (blender CSC) and DE33 (channel CSC) so RGB
to YUV conversion works for them too.

Since the DE3 blender CSC units are always enabled, program an
identity matrix at the output encoding when no conversion is needed.
This also fixes stale coefficients being applied when a channel
switches from a YUV format to an RGB one.

Background and bottom plane fill color are now set according to the
output format, since their values are interpreted in the output color
space.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
